# ============================================================
# flow/antenna_starved_partner.buda
#
# The CONTROL for flow/antenna_culled_partner.buda: identical
# design, identical pin, one number different in the keepout —
# and the dangling metal is gone.
#
# There are two ways to lose a partner segment at DetailedNUTS,
# and they sit on opposite sides of `adjust_bit_spans`:
#
#   place_by_layer   -- STARVED: no eligible track, the bits are
#                       counted unplaced and never created
#         |
#   adjust_bit_spans -- the neighbour extends to reach whatever
#                       partner bits EXIST at this moment
#         |
#   cull_keepout_    -- CULLED: bits that were placed, and were
#     crossers          extended to, are deleted afterwards
#
# STARVED (here) is benign: by the time spans are adjusted the
# partner is already absent, so #678's stale-end rule fires and
# the neighbour retracts to its own via —
#
#   seg1 bit0  M4 track=399.5  span=[183.5,183.5]   <- retracted
#   detailed WL 807, no antenna findings
#
# CULLED (the twin) dangles: the partner is deleted one pass too
# late, after the neighbour was already stretched to meet it —
#
#   seg1 bit0  M4  span=[183.5,710]  reaches [183.5,183.5]
#   detailed WL 2922, of which 2115 reaches nothing
#
# THAT CONTRAST IS THE POINT OF THIS FILE.  Same blocks, same
# candidate, same bits, same keepout rectangle except for its
# top edge.  So the cause is not the keepout and not the
# geometry — it is WHERE IN THE PASS ORDER the partner goes.
# Whichever way that is fixed (retract after the cull, or cull
# before adjusting), this vehicle is what must not regress.
#
# The keepout here spans y 380..720, covering seg2's span
# MIDPOINT (y=500).  `signal_tracks_in` tests a keepout at that
# single sample point, so the pool comes back empty and
# placement fails admission:
#
#   [DetailedNUTS] Warning: Layer 5 has insufficient signal
#   tracks (0) for bus width 4 in interval [710, 790]
#
# num_keepout_bits is 0 here and 4 in the twin — that counter is
# how a test tells the two paths apart, and asserting on
# num_unplaced alone cannot (it is 4 either way).
#
# Ends DIRTY on purpose (4 unplaced bits).  Not for the corpus.
#
# Run:  bin/buda flow/antenna_starved_partner.buda --no-viz
# ============================================================

def_layer 4 M4 H TOP 33.33
def_layer 5 M5 V TOP 33.33

corner_margin dx 10 dy 10

add_block drv  100 100  200 200
add_block rcv  700 600  800 700

add_bus b[4] drv.tx rcv.rx

run_bundler strict
generate_topologies

# Candidate 4 is Z_VHV@y400@x190, as in the twin.
select_topology 1 4

run_planner 1
run_nuts

def_track_pattern 4 0  POWER 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4  GROUND 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4
def_track_pattern 5 0  POWER 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4  GROUND 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4

# The twin's keepout with its top edge at 720 instead of 450:
# now it covers seg2's span midpoint, so admission fails.
add_keepout 600 380 900 720 5

run_detailed_nuts
dump_topologies --conn
check_design dnuts
report_wirelength
